Subject: [PATCH RFC] spi: geni-qcom: log pre-initialization engine state

Collect the existing protocol, firmware revision, interface-disable,
clock-status and hardware-parameter registers immediately after the
existing runtime-PM acquire, before protocol dispatch or any firmware
load. This temporary diagnostic allows the image collector to read the
journal without direct MMIO access or triggering a second probe.

Only read-only status registers already defined by the GENI header are
sampled. No transfer, firmware request, protocol predicate or register
write is added. A disabled DT controller will not produce this message:
the kernel/image owners must arrange the next controller-only diagnostic
boot. Do not enable the HID child or add firmware-name to obtain this
evidence.

This RFC is unbuilt and excluded from the integration series. Remove the
instrumentation after the boot evidence is captured.

Assisted-by: Codex gpt-6.1-sol
---
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -640,6 +640,14 @@
 	}
 
 	proto = geni_se_read_proto(se);
+	dev_info(mas->dev,
+		 "touch-pen-diag: proto=%u fw=%#010x if_disable=%#x clk=%#x hw0=%#x hw1=%#x hw2=%#x\n",
+		 proto, readl(se->base + GENI_FW_REVISION_RO),
+		 readl(se->base + GENI_IF_DISABLE_RO),
+		 readl(se->base + GENI_CLK_CTRL_RO),
+		 readl(se->base + SE_HW_PARAM_0),
+		 readl(se->base + SE_HW_PARAM_1),
+		 readl(se->base + SE_HW_PARAM_2));
 
 	if (spi->target) {
 		if (proto != GENI_SE_SPI_SLAVE) {
